{
  "format": "optibench-workstation",
  "version": 1,
  "meta": {
    "appVersion": "0.1.0-alpha",
    "author": "Optibench examples",
    "created": "2026-11-19T00:00:00.000Z",
    "description": "A 5 mW red laser is focused by an f = 25 mm plano-convex lens into the 200 um core of a 10 m silica multimode fibre (NA 0.22; the beam NA is only ~0.04, well inside the acceptance cone). The fibre end B is routed to a second bench position where the light exits as a cone and is caught by a power meter. Losses: Fresnel reflection at the lens and both fibre faces plus ~5 dB/km attenuation. Move the fibre face away from the focus (or lower the NA) to watch the coupling drop.",
    "dimension": "2d",
    "modified": "2026-11-19T00:00:00.000Z",
    "title": "Fiber Link"
  },
